{
  "profile": "tabular-data-package",
  "name": "weatheo-city-climate-pt",
  "title": "Portugal city daily weather 1950-2025 and climate indicators (ERA5-Land)",
  "description": "Daily weather 1950-2025, monthly climate, climate normals 1991-2020 and annual climate indicators 1951-2025 for the 20 largest cities of Portugal, from the Copernicus ERA5-Land hourly time series. Cities: in France and Germany the most populous municipalities by official population (INSEE, BKG), one point per municipality (city districts are not counted separately); elsewhere the most populous GeoNames places, skipping a place in the same 0.1 deg cell and district as a larger one. Each city takes the ERA5-Land time series (0.1 deg) of the grid cell at its GeoNames point, or of a neighbouring land cell when that cell is sea. Hourly values are grouped into local civil days (the city's IANA time zone); only complete days are kept. Temperatures are adjusted from the cell elevation to the city elevation with 6.5 degC per km. Wind is the mean of hourly 10 m wind speeds, not gusts. Monthly and annual values use complete months and years only. The daily series start on 2 January 1950 (3 January in time zones ahead of UTC) and the monthly series in February 1950: the hourly series are downloaded from 00:00 UTC on 2 January 1950 and only complete local days are kept. Values are reanalysis grid-cell values adjusted for altitude, not station observations: they can differ from official station normals, mostly near coasts, in cities and in steep terrain. Daily extremes are smoothed: on record heat days the daily maximum is often 2 to 7 degC below the station record (London, 19 July 2022: 36.4 degC here, 40.2 degC measured at Coningsby). Contains modified Copernicus Climate Change Service information 2026. Neither the European Commission nor ECMWF is responsible for any use that may be made of the Copernicus information or data it contains.",
  "version": "1.1.0",
